course: dictionary
lesson: 3212
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. Enlightenment is a good example. In everyday speech it means finally understanding something that puzzled you. In a religious text it means something very different. «Wesak is when many Buddhists remember the Buddha's birth, enlightenment and death.» This sentence is about religion, so enlightenment here means a state of perfect understanding and peace.
explain: Look at the topic first. In a history lesson, the Enlightenment with a capital E is a time in Europe in the 1700s when thinkers said people should use reason, science and evidence, and question old ideas. «The Age of Enlightenment» is the name for that time. A capital letter is a clue too, because it shows a name or a special time.
explain: When you meet an unknown meaning, ask: what word would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense. If it does not, try another meaning, or look the word up in a dictionary.
fact: Enlightenment is a noun. It can mean gaining knowledge, or understanding something clearly after it was puzzling.
fact: The Enlightenment was a time in Europe in the 1700s when thinkers used reason, science and evidence.
fact: In Buddhism, enlightenment is a state of perfect understanding and peace that the Buddha is believed to have reached.
fact: «Seek enlightenment» means look for understanding, and «for your enlightenment» is a humorous phrase used to introduce an explanation.
fact: Scientists and thinkers such as Isaac Newton, Voltaire and Benjamin Franklin are linked with the Enlightenment.
exercise: «Wesak is when many Buddhists remember the Buddha's birth, enlightenment and death.» Which meaning fits here? | A time in Europe in the 1700s | Lighting lamps in the autumn | *A state of perfect understanding and peace | Finishing a long walk
exercise: Ella reads, «The Enlightenment changed how people thought about science.» What does Enlightenment mean here? | A quiet, sad mood | A bright light shining in the sky | *A time in Europe in the 1700s when thinkers used reason and evidence | Feeling very hungry after a walk
exercise: Jayden says, «I finally get it, enlightenment at last!» What does enlightenment mean in everyday speech? | Wearing bright clothes | Being very tired | Going on holiday | *Finally understanding something that puzzled you
test: «The Age of Enlightenment» is a phrase from which lesson? | *History | Games | Music | Maths
test: Why does the word enlightenment have different meanings in different texts? | Because dictionaries are always wrong | Because the context, such as the topic and capital letters, shows which meaning is used | *Because the context tells you which meaning fits | Because every word means the same thing
exam: Read «Wesak is when many Buddhists remember the Buddha's birth, enlightenment and death.» What does enlightenment mean here, and which clue in the sentence helps you decide? | Gaining knowledge in a history class | Being very hungry | A bright light | *A state of perfect understanding and peace, because the sentence is about Buddhists and the Buddha
